# Push and PR Delivery

- After completing and verifying an implementation, commit only the changes that belong to the requested work.
- Push the commit to an appropriately named remote branch and create a pull request targeting `main`.
- If a pull request for the active branch already exists, update that pull request instead of creating a duplicate.
- Do not include unrelated or unfinished user changes in the commit.
- Report the branch name, commit hash, and pull request link when delivery finishes.
- If authentication, conflicts, or repository policy prevents push or PR creation, report the exact blocker instead of silently stopping.
